Mu-Silicium: break the PcdDxe self-deadlock on enchilada

Applies AFTER mu-silicium-unixnu-integration.patch (its anchor is the
DarwinBoot !endif block that patch adds).

PcdDxe (DXE_DRIVER) links DxePcdLib, whose [Depex] is gEfiPcdProtocolGuid.
BaseTools merges library depex into the module depex unconditionally, so the
as-built depex of PcdDxe becomes "PUSH gEfiPcdProtocolGuid END" - the driver
waits for the very protocol it installs and never dispatches. Every driver
whose depex references gEfiPcdProtocolGuid (29 modules incl. VariableRuntimeDxe,
RealTimeClock, ResetSystem, Metronome, CapsuleRuntimeDxe, UniXNUDxe) then
stays undispatched, the architectural protocols never appear and DxeCore
asserts at DxeMain.c(581). Observed on-device 2026-11-07.

Override PcdLib with BasePcdLibNull for Pcd.inf exactly like upstream
OvmfPkgX64.dsc does for the same module.
---
--- a/Platforms/OnePlus/enchiladaPkg/enchilada.dsc
+++ b/Platforms/OnePlus/enchiladaPkg/enchilada.dsc
@@ -91,3 +91,15 @@
   UniXNUPkg/Driver/UniXNURamDiskDxe/UniXNURamDiskDxe.inf
   DarwinBootPkg/Driver/DarwinBoot.inf
 !endif
+
+  #
+  # PcdDxe must use BasePcdLibNull: BaseTools merges DxePcdLib's
+  # gEfiPcdProtocolGuid depex into the module depex, so PcdDxe would wait for
+  # the protocol it itself installs and never dispatch, starving every
+  # PCD-dependent driver (VariableRuntimeDxe, RTC, Capsule, ...) and tripping
+  # DxeMain.c(581). Same override upstream OvmfPkgX64.dsc makes for Pcd.inf.
+  #
+  MdeModulePkg/Universal/PCD/Dxe/Pcd.inf {
+    <LibraryClasses>
+      PcdLib|MdePkg/Library/BasePcdLibNull/BasePcdLibNull.inf
+  }
